nd had 5 drinks within an few hours including 2 shots. I hate to tell her this but no man is going to drug you with a drug that turns you into a crazy bitch. He's going to drug you with something that makes you docile and easy to fuck. She was with friends so I doubt any man is going to target her anyway. </p>\n<p>Guys, I think she's just a bitch that couldn't hide that she's a bitch cause she was drunk.</p>"],[1,9433475,0,0,0,0,"2017-06-07T11:35:18","nocuckcanuck","",[],"<p>CNN says &quot;come on over&quot;...you've got the titties.</p>"]]
[[0,1916232,0,2,0,2,"2017-06-07T01:08:04","SmExyGLazeRZ184","[e]",[],"<p>Im relativly new, so im not sure how to link images. But here are some tips on Firearm usage. This is a response to <a href=\"https://voat.co/user/Rainy-Day-Dream\">@Rainy-Day-Dream</a> and their post about self defense. I dont know as much as other marksmen, but I know enough to get by. </p>\n<p>First and foermost is saftey. In general, most ranges and other people (especially trained individuals) appreciate it when you keep your finger off of the trigger until you are ready to fire. Keeping the end of the barrel pointed away from anything you dont intend to shoot is a must. This ensures the safety of yourself and the individuals around you (unless you are defending yourself). Keep the safety on at all times, and dont disengage it untill you are ready to fire.</p>\n<p>Know your local ranges rules before you go, and be curteous. If they want you to pick up your expended casings (brass), do it. This helps keep the range open and clean for other users. Dont be that dick who leaves their brass everywhere.</p>\n<p>Know your states regulation and laws on lawfully carrying a weapon for selfe defense, as well as any laws pretaining to weapon and magazine restrictions (my condolances to Cuckifornia). Some people/officers may try and pull some BS that is illegal, enen if youve done nothing wrong. Knowlege is power.</p>\n<p>When at a range and you want to check your target, make sure everyone is aware of your intentions. Leave your firearm on the table with the chamber/bolt open when checking targets. Use and empty chamber flag if you have one. </p>\n<p>Be aware of your surroundings when practicing. Don't shoot animals on the range, as most ranges will ban you for this. Don't shoot in the air like some sandnigger muslim, you will be banned and/or arrested for improper use of a deadly weapon (not sure what it is actually called). </p>\n<p>When transporting firearms, it is best to keep them in a box or gun case, unloaded (laws vary state to state). Safe transportation of firearms is important, as it will (mostly) keep you out of trouble with the law. </p>\n<p>If you conceal carry and find yourself in a traffic stop, KEEP YOU HANDS ON THE WHEEL and comply woth the officers. The way they see it, they would rather defend themselves in court rather than be dead, so they will not hesitate to shoot.</p>\n<p>If you find yourself in an active shooter/hostage situation, when you pull that trigger, be prepared to spend the money hiring a lawyer. Also, when it blows over and the police roll in, comply with what they saw and lay down your weapon, if they tell you to (they probably will). If you refuse, or you try and act in a way that could be interpreted as threatening, they will not hesitate to shoot you. Remember, they most likely dont know who the active shooter and who the law abiding citizen is if both are armed. They will only see you as a threat. </p>\n<p>Lastly, the common criminal/thug is usually deterred if have put if you have a gun of your own, so you may not even need to fire. This does not pretain to every situation, and it is useful to know how to read a situation. Personally, if they have a gun and you can draw yours, fire. Youll probably be safe from most legal action. </p>\n<p>I hopes this helps. Also, feef free to grammer nazi me, as my spelling is horrific. Remember voaters, stay safe, and tread lightly. We live in troubled times.</p>","In response to @Rainy-Day-Dream, Here are some basic tips on firearm usage.","","TheDonald"],[1,9431199,0,0,0,0,"2017-06-07T04:14:53","eyeVoated","",[],"<p>In other words: Take a firearms safety course </p>"],[1,9434084,0,0,0,0,"2017-06-07T12:53:54","Dfens","",[],"<p>I'm not sure I agree about shotguns not being the best form of home protection. They are very lethal and when people are in panic mode they tend to need that buckshot spread to hit a target. AR-15s, on the other hand, make small holes, the rounds don't have much energy, and those muzzle breaks make the noise at the shooter's end very loud and unnerving. </p>"]]
